# Python Quality Standards

- Target Python 3.12. Use modern syntax (PEP 604 unions `X | None`, builtin
  generics `list[str]`, `type` statements where appropriate).
- All functions and methods must have complete type annotations, including
  return types. The codebase must pass `mypy --strict`.
- Code must pass `ruff check .` and `ruff format --check .` before completion.
- No `print()` in library code under `src/`; use logging when it is introduced.
  Scripts under `scripts/` may print.
- Public modules, classes, and functions get concise docstrings that state
  intent, not restate the signature.
- Do not add placeholder implementations that pretend to work; unimplemented
  paths must be explicit (e.g. raise `NotImplementedError`).
